From 57e5f4a111dbd9739a0fc77f93bcf49e4df1080e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gilles <62951130+VivaLaVent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:14:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Count BLS boots

Entries named name+LEFT-DONE.conf are renamed to +(LEFT-1)-(DONE+1) after the kernel and initrd are read, keeping the digit widths as the spec asks. Entries at +0 are skipped instead of sorted last, so the loader aborts when no other entry is left. Marking an entry good is left to the OS. The loader.conf default matches the entry name without its counter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
